    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can personalize math lessons by adapting to individual learning speeds, offering step-by-step explanations for tricky topics, and generating practice problems tailored to student weaknesses. They could also create interactive simulations for abstract concepts, making math more engaging and accessible without overwhelming beginners."
